   "title": {
    "zh": "装得下吗",
    "en": "Does It Fit?"
   },
   "why": {
    "zh": "从两人座的缆车讲起：再要好，也得装得下。然后是同样的五个朋友、同样的合并规则，只是座位有限：双座车装不下五个人（不可能），两把大提琴让出租车走进死胡同（卡住），双人自行车上最要好的一对反而拆散最多（不是最好）。",
    "en": "It opens on a two-seat chairlift: however close, it has to fit. Then the same five friends and the same merge rule, but seats are limited: two-seaters cannot take five in two cars (impossible), two cellos lead the taxis into a dead end (stuck), and on tandem bikes the closest pair splits the most (not the best)."
   },
