      {
       "start": 3.4,
       "end": 11.978,
       "text": "The rule is Module 03's, plus one line: a cluster's total size may not exceed the capacity C.",
       "sceneId": "k01-problem"
      },
      {
       "start": 11.978,
       "end": 16.556,
       "text": "At capacity 2 and K = 2, G01 stops at 3 clusters.",
       "sceneId": "k01-problem"
      },
      {
       "start": 16.556,
       "end": 25.133,
       "text": "The report: legal, but K is not reached; the stop reason is capacity-blocked.",
       "sceneId": "k01-problem"
      },
      {
       "start": 25.133,
       "end": 29.2,
       "text": "The four are independent; report them separately.",
       "sceneId": "k01-problem"
      },
      {
       "start": 29.6,
       "end": 36.844,
       "text": "One graph: at capacity 3, AB plus C is 3, legal, giving ABC | DE.",
       "sceneId": "k02-fork"
      },
      {
       "start": 36.844,
       "end": 43.2,
       "text": "At capacity 2, the highest-affinity AB–C is blocked, so D–E instead.",
       "sceneId": "k02-fork"
      },
      {
       "start": 43.2,
       "end": 49.556,
       "text": "After that both candidates are 3: it stops at AB | C | DE, cut 8.",
       "sceneId": "k02-fork"
      },
      {
       "start": 49.956,
       "end": 53.889,
       "text": "Is that greedy's fault? First, the lower bound.",
       "sceneId": "k03-bound"
      },
      {
       "start": 53.889,
       "end": 58.489,
       "text": "Total size 5, at most 2 per cluster: at least 3 clusters.",
       "sceneId": "k03-bound"
      },
      {
       "start": 58.489,
       "end": 63.289,
       "text": "K = 2 is impossible; no algorithm can do it.",
       "sceneId": "k03-bound"
      },
      {
       "start": 63.289,
       "end": 68.089,
       "text": "But a bound only proves impossible, never possible.",
       "sceneId": "k03-bound"
      },
      {
       "start": 68.489,
       "end": 76.844,
       "text": "The original author's greedy_trap: A and B have size 2, capacity 3, and the bound allows two clusters.",
       "sceneId": "k04-trap"
      },
      {
       "start": 76.844,
       "end": 80.311,
       "text": "Greedy merges the biggest, C–D, first.",
       "sceneId": "k04-trap"
      },
      {
       "start": 80.311,
       "end": 84.444,
       "text": "Then neither A nor B fits: it stops at 3 clusters.",
       "sceneId": "k04-trap"
      },
      {
       "start": 84.444,
       "end": 90.133,
       "text": "Yet exhaustive search finds AC | BD: feasible, but greedy is stuck.",
       "sceneId": "k04-trap"
      },
      {
       "start": 90.533,
       "end": 97.111,
       "text": "The suboptimal graph: greedy merges A–B first, the largest at 10.",
       "sceneId": "k05-sub"
      },
      {
       "start": 97.111,
       "end": 101.022,
       "text": "Both 9s stay in the cut: 18.",
       "sceneId": "k05-sub"
      },
      {
       "start": 101.022,
       "end": 106.044,
       "text": "The legal AC | BD cuts only 10 and 1: 11.",
       "sceneId": "k05-sub"
      },
      {
       "start": 106.044,
       "end": 110.844,
       "text": "Both legal, both reach K; greedy just isn't optimal.",
       "sceneId": "k05-sub"
      },
      {
       "start": 111.244,
       "end": 116.489,
       "text": "Node sizes change the ending too: set A's size to 2.",
       "sceneId": "k06-uneven"
      },
      {
       "start": 116.489,
       "end": 120.178,
       "text": "After A–B it is full, and C does not fit.",
       "sceneId": "k06-uneven"
      },
      {
       "start": 120.178,
       "end": 126.089,
       "text": "The result becomes AB | CDE, cut 5. Capacity counts area.",
       "sceneId": "k06-uneven"
      },
      {
       "start": 126.489,
       "end": 128.622,
       "text": "Four things to keep.",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      },
      {
       "start": 128.622,
       "end": 133.089,
       "text": "Filter first, then take the largest; report four items;",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      },
      {
       "start": 133.089,
       "end": 136.333,
       "text": "a bound above K means impossible;",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      },
      {
       "start": 136.333,
       "end": 142.467,
       "text": "stuck and not optimal need a comparison with search. Try it in the lab below.",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      }
     ],
